# Per-machine configuration for k3s-bootstrap. NOT committed (see .gitignore).
#
#   cp scripts/config.local.sh.example scripts/config.local.sh
#   $EDITOR scripts/config.local.sh
#
# This is the ONE host-specific file the cluster needs. Everything else that
# defines the cluster (agents, DNS, egress, VM size, mounts) lives in the
# config repo it points at.

# REQUIRED. Absolute path to your cloned config repo on this machine.
# Clone the template (k3s-bootstrap-config-template), make it private, edit it,
# then point here. '~' is expanded.
CONFIG_REPO_ROOT="${HOME}/usr/src/k3s-bootstrap-config"

# OPTIONAL per-machine VM-size overrides. Leave commented to use the values
# committed in the config repo's cluster.conf. Uncomment only when this Mac
# needs different sizing (e.g. a smaller laptop). These take precedence over
# cluster.conf. NOTE: changing any of these after the VM exists requires a
# teardown + setup (setup.sh will refuse to start otherwise).
# CPUS=4
# MEMORY=16
# DISK=100
